  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Thirty-One (Greek). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Thirty-One (often called '31' or 'H τριανταμία' in Greek) is a simple draw-and-discard game popular in Greece and worldwide. Players try to collect a hand of three cards in the same suit totaling 31 points (Ace=11, Face=10). The player with the lowest score loses a life.",
    objective: 'Get a hand totaling 31 points in one suit, or have a higher score than the lowest player.',
    gameplay: 'Turn: Draw one card from Stock or Discard pile, then discard one card. Try to improve suit sum. Knocking: If a player thinks they have high enough score, they knock. Everyone else gets one last turn. Scoring: A=11, K/Q/J=10, Num=Face. 3 of a kind (30pts) is a special rule in some variants.',
    keyRules: [
      'Suits matters (points must be same suit)',
      'Ace = 11',
      'Knocking ends the round (after 1 orbit)',
      '31 is instant win',
    ],
